course: dictionary
lesson: 15146
title: Planned and on time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Scheduled means planned to happen at a certain time. «The train is scheduled to leave at 9:15» tells you the train has a plan, and the plan says 9:15. The time is your clue: when you see a time or a day, something has probably been scheduled.
explain: Schedule is the verb, and scheduled is its past form. Mum scheduled the dentist for Tuesday means she put the visit on a plan or list. As an adjective, a scheduled flight is one that runs on a regular timetable, like the bus that leaves every hour.
explain: Check the meaning by swapping in a word. «The train is planned to leave at 9:15» still makes sense, so planned is a good match for scheduled. If the swap makes the sentence silly, go back and read the clues again.
fact: Scheduled means planned to happen at a certain time.
fact: Scheduled is the past tense and past participle of schedule.
fact: A scheduled flight is a flight that runs on a regular plan or timetable.
fact: In maths, a bus scheduled for 10:40 that runs 15 minutes late comes at 10:55.
fact: Words like "at", "for" and "to", along with a time or day, often show that something is scheduled.
exercise: «The concert is scheduled for 7 o'clock.» What does scheduled mean here? | Cancelled forever | *Planned to happen at a certain time | Very loud | Lost on the way
exercise: «The bus was scheduled to arrive at 10:40, but it came at 10:55.» How many minutes late was the bus? | 25 minutes | *15 minutes | 45 minutes | 10 minutes
exercise: Which word could replace scheduled in «The train is scheduled to leave at 9:15»? | hidden | *planned | forgotten | painted
test: «Ella scheduled her swimming lesson for 4 o'clock.» What did Ella do? | Forgot about it completely | Swam in the sea at lunchtime | *Put it on her plan for 4 o'clock
test: What does a scheduled flight mean? | A flight that is very fast | *A flight on a regular plan or timetable | A flight that was lost | A flight with no pilot
exam: Which sentence means the same as "The meeting is planned for noon"? | The meeting is forgotten at noon. | The meeting is hidden at noon. | *The meeting is scheduled for noon. | The meeting is painted for noon.
